#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185006} :activity/id #uuid "af91633b-288c-52bd-a641-7172621608f6" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049327 :topic/id #uuid "ec1d59b5-66a8-5507-9862-10567e3ce6ab" :topic/math-academy-id 3834} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184944 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184177 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184078 :question/id #uuid "7dbb258d-fe71-5e7b-9501-c88ffdb6fe86" :question/math-academy-id "e-629"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2216cdfc-7f2a-5c53-b10b-2d66f35fbf32" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050162} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050277}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184535} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184796} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527917}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Tangent Lines to Polar Curves"} :step/id #uuid "a0ead2f8-7726-5a22-ad4d-582c7b4b8968" :step/math-academy-id 2206 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185001}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185001 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184215 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184120 :question/id #uuid "59156f24-72a1-5642-ac66-f84002c87d0b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9955"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e95ede7-306b-55e1-9245-7493f0afb514" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184437} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184536}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Normal Lines to Polar Curves"} :step/id #uuid "e6c2d34a-6683-50c4-a82e-b71e985d4ed8" :step/math-academy-id 37487} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185006 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185342 :tutorial/content "![](images/a0/a0b4ad67ea80f6d6eec3a15b3df18d551d84263c7424405588bd15162ef4e7c2.png)\n\nThe polar curve shown above is defined as\n\n$$\nr(\\theta) = 4 - 3\\cos \\theta, \\qquad 0\\leq \\theta < 2\\pi\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nat the point $P$. The tangent to the curve at $P$ is shown in the diagram.\n\nTo find the equation of the tangent line to the curve at $P$, we follow four steps.\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nUsing techniques that we've previously discussed, we can show that\n\n$$\ny^{′}(θ) = 4\\cos θ - 3\\cos 2θ, x^{′}(θ) = 3\\sin 2θ - 4\\sin θ\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can find\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= (y^{′}(θ))/(x^{′}(θ)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{4\\cos θ - 3\\cos 2θ}{3\\sin 2θ - 4\\sin θ}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P$.\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{θ = π/2} \\\\\n&= (4\\cos (\\frac{π}{2}) - 3\\cos (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{2}))/(3\\sin (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{2}) - 4\\sin (\\frac{π}{2})) \\\\\n&= (4\\cos (\\frac{π}{2}) - 3\\cos (π))/(3\\sin (π) - 4\\sin (\\frac{π}{2})) \\\\\n&= \\frac{0 + 3}{0 - 4} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P$.\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1} &= r\\cos θ \\\\\n&= (4 - 3\\cos θ)\\cos θ \\\\\n&= (4 - 3\\cos (\\frac{π}{2}))\\cos (\\frac{π}{2}) \\\\\n&= 0 \\\\\ny_{1} &= r\\sin θ \\\\\n&= (4 - 3\\cos θ)\\sin θ \\\\\n&= (4 - 3\\cos (\\frac{π}{2}))\\sin (\\frac{π}{2}) \\\\\n&= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are\n\n$$\n\\left(0, 4 \\right)\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the tangent.\n\nWe find the equation of the tangent as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - 4 &= -\\frac{3}{4} \\cdot (x - 0) \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{3}{4}x + 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "febc7b49-9662-5e78-a7a5-cbe9b1f596ba" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6186 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "a1e51e4b-71cf-5749-aae1-c001b3a5a59b" :step/math-academy-id 37501 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184944}}] :activity/title "Tangent and Normal Lines to Polar Curves" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186184419}]}
